 Does a bulk TRB whose data buffer crosses a 64 KB boundary work on a
 spec-strict controller? xHCI is believed to forbid it, and msc-read-into
 pushes a single 32 KB Normal TRB at whatever address the caller passed,
 so on most boots the seed read issues about thirty crossing TRBs.

 The same LBA is read twice: once into a buffer on a 64 KB boundary,
 where a 32 KB transfer cannot cross, and once into a buffer starting
 1024 bytes below one, where it must. Both the return code and a
 checksum of the delivered bytes are reported, because a controller that
 accepts the TRB and moves the wrong bytes is the outcome a return code
 alone would hide.

 A third read at an out-of-range LBA is the liveness check on the
 failure channel: if that does not report failure, then a pass on the
 other two says nothing, because nothing here can report anything.

 We say:

  probe-halt : Integer -> Integer
  probe-halt (n) = probe-halt (n + 1)

  pnib : Integer -> Text
  pnib (n) =
    if n == 0 then "0" else if n == 1 then "1" else if n == 2 then "2"
    else if n == 3 then "3" else if n == 4 then "4" else if n == 5 then "5"
    else if n == 6 then "6" else if n == 7 then "7" else if n == 8 then "8"
    else if n == 9 then "9" else if n == 10 then "a" else if n == 11 then "b"
    else if n == 12 then "c" else if n == 13 then "d" else if n == 14 then "e"
    else "f"

  phx : Integer, Integer -> Text
  phx (v) (sh) = pnib (bit-and (bit-shru v sh) 15)

  phw : Integer -> Text
  phw (v) = phx v 28 & phx v 24 & phx v 20 & phx v 16 & phx v 12 & phx v 8 & phx v 4 & phx v 0

  ph64 : Integer -> Text
  ph64 (v) = "#" & phw (bit-shru v 32) & "_" & phw v

  pyn : Integer -> Text
  pyn (v) = if v == 0 then "n" else "y"

 The liveness LBA is DERIVED from the medium, not written down. It was the
 literal 100000, which is out of range on the 16 MB emulator image and well
 inside a 28.9 GB stick, so on the ASUS 2026-08-04 the arm read `ok=y` and
 the probe correctly announced that it proved nothing. A constant that
 encodes the bed's disk size is not a liveness check anywhere else.

 Sixty-four dwords spread across the 32 KB at a 512-byte stride. Enough
 to catch a short, shifted or absent transfer without walking every byte.

  chk : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  chk (a) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 64 then acc
    else chk a (i + 1) (acc + peek-32 a (i * 512))

  prow : Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, Integer, Text, Integer -> Integer
  prow (base) (stride) (font) (y) (scale) (s) (col) =
    gop-draw-text base stride font 40 y s col scale 0

 blu's ASDE stage rides here rather than on its own boot, because the body
 at the bench is the expensive line and these two arms cost no extra flash.

 THEY MUST STAY LAST. This stage is unproven on metal -- that is what the
 flight is for -- and the four rows above it answer a storage question that
 cost a board trip to ask. Painted first, those rows survive an ASDE arm
 that faults or hangs on the real part.

 Two breadcrumbs, because on the ASUS 2026-08-04 NO ASDE row appeared at
 all. Every non-crashing path prints something, so the silence proved only
 that something between entry and the first row died -- it could not say
 whether the scan, the BAR read or the bring-up, nor name the device chosen.
 One row before the scan and one naming the eligible device make those three
 distinguishable, and both survive a fault or a hang beneath them.

 The candidate is looked for on bus 0 because the I219 is a PCH-integrated
 MAC at 00:1f.6. That scope is stated ON the miss row rather than left
 implicit: a scan that finds nothing must not photograph the same as a bus
 that was never searched. `na-eligible` is blu's vendor-plus-BAR gate and
 the Realtek at 06:00.0 is what it exists to reject, because Intel register
 offsets read off that part yield garbage shaped like an answer.

  na-rows : Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer -> [Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Integer
  na-rows (base) (stride) (font) (scale) =
    let bc0 = prow base stride font 240 scale "ASDE: scanning bus 0" 9474192
    in let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in when e1000-find scan
      is None -> prow base stride font 270 scale "ASDE: no Intel NIC on bus 0 (scope: bus 0 only)" 16755200
      is Just (dev) ->
        if na-eligible dev == False
        then prow base stride font 270 scale "ASDE: candidate REJECTED by vendor/BAR gate" 16755200
        else let bc1 = prow base stride font 270 scale ("ASDE: eligible at " & show (dev.pci-bus) & ":" & show (dev.pci-dev) & "." & show (dev.pci-func) & " -- entering bring-up") 16776960
        in let mmio = na-mmio-of dev
        in let on = na-bring-up mmio True
        in let off = na-bring-up mmio False
        in let r1 = prow base stride font 300 scale (na-line "ASDE=1" on) 65280
        in prow base stride font 330 scale (na-line "ASDE=0" off) 65280

  opening : [Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Integer
  opening =
    let base = boot-fb-base 0
    in let w = boot-fb-w 0
    in let h = boot-fb-h 0
    in let stride = boot-fb-stride 0
    in let font = cbf-init
    in let scale = if w >= 1024 then 2 else 1
    in act
      ri <- runtime-init 0
      att <- usb-attach
      let hp = __heap-save
      in let adv = __heap-advance 262144
      in let al = hp + (65536 - int-mod hp 65536)
      in let xa = al + 64512
      in let d = att.ua-disk
      in let ra = msc-read-into d 0 64 al
      in let cha = chk al 0 0
      in let rc = msc-read-into d 0 64 xa
      in let chc = chk xa 0 0
      in let badlba = (d.md-sectors) + 16
      in let ro = msc-read-into d badlba 64 al
      in let bg = gop-fill-rect base stride 0 0 w h 1710638
      in let t0 = prow base stride font 40 scale "MSC 64K BOUNDARY PROBE" 65535
      in let t1 = prow base stride font 80 scale ("disk=" & pyn (if (d.md-ok) then 1 else 0) & " sectors=" & show (d.md-sectors) & "  heap=" & ph64 hp & " heap mod 64K=" & show (int-mod hp 65536)) 9474192
      in let t2 = prow base stride font 110 scale ("ALIGNED  addr=" & ph64 al & " off=" & show (int-mod al 65536) & " ok=" & pyn ra & " chk=" & phw cha) 65280
      in let t3 = prow base stride font 140 scale ("CROSSING addr=" & ph64 xa & " off=" & show (int-mod xa 65536) & " ok=" & pyn rc & " chk=" & phw chc) 65280
      in let t4 = prow base stride font 170 scale ("data identical=" & pyn (if cha == chc then 1 else 0) & "   (same LBA, both 64 sectors)") 16776960
      in let t5 = prow base stride font 200 scale ("LIVENESS lba=" & show badlba & " (sectors+16) ok=" & pyn ro & "  must be n, or the two rows above prove nothing") 16776960
      in act
        t6 <- na-rows base stride font scale
        probe-halt 0
      end
    end
